
# 14. Bin Sort

## Question Description
Implement Bin Sort in C++ to arrange integers in ascending order. Bin Sort distributes elements into bins based on their values, then collects the elements in order. This implementation assumes non-negative integers within a known range.

## Test Cases

### Test Case 1
Input: `[4, 2, 7, 1, 3]`

Expected Output:
`[1, 2, 3, 4, 7]`

### Test Case 2
Input: `[9, 5, 3, 7, 1]`

Expected Output:
`[1, 3, 5, 7, 9]`

### Test Case 3
Input: `[4, 4, 2, 1, 2]`

Expected Output:
`[1, 2, 2, 4, 4]`

## Time Complexity
- O(n + k), where n is the number of elements and k is the size of the value range, for a counting-style bin implementation.

## Space Complexity
- O(n + k)
